      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify that dose. At that level the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **The dose is a typo.** If you meant 50 mg or 100 mg daily, or 200 mg at most, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. Usual dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily and is titrated in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least a week.\n2. **The dose is intentional.** This could be a specialist-directed regimen for refractory illness. If so, please confirm that you know it's above the labeled maximum, and give me the clinical rationale to put in the order note. I can then enter it with a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max; confirmed by attending.\" Your institution may also require pharmacy review or an override for this.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
